From 6406aa8896064ae0a6e984fce8d0c7c42e862954 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 02:37:17 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] GRPO from the KD student: Dr. GRPO advantages switch,
 launcher defaults

GRPO.advantage_std_normalize (default True = historical) selects between the
release advantage (r - mean) / (std + 1e-8) and plain r - mean.  With the
release normalisation a group whose 8 samples all succeed and differ only in
SPL / NE gets the same unit-scale advantages as a group split between
success and failure; for a student that already succeeds on most train_10
episodes those groups dominate the update and push toward shorter paths
rather than more arrivals (R7 iter17000 GRPO continuation: PL -0.9 m, steps
-7, SR -1.25 vs its DAgger parent).  Two group diagnostics are logged either
way: grpo/group_reward_std and grpo/group_all_success.

run_grpo_from_dagger.sh: DAGGER_RUN defaults to kd_dual (the 67.26 SR
student); defaults restored to the release GRPO transition (nav4, LR 2e-5,
500 iters, seed 100, cosine to 0.25x, beta 0.04, G=8) instead of the
iter17000 continuation values (2e-6 / seed 10 / 800); new ADV_STD_NORM env
(default False -> Dr. GRPO advantages, True reproduces the release); run name
gets _advstd / _<profile> suffixes for the non-default arms.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
